{
  "about": "The say messages (docs/network/02-link-protocol.md section 9): the hub asks a world to say a line as one of its characters, a line the character's person said elsewhere, and the world's answer. Every `ok` frame must read as its type, and a write of what was read must hold every field of the frame with the same value and read back unchanged; where an `ok` case gives `expect`, the message read must have those field values (`reason` null when left out). Every `later` frame must read, leaving out what it adds, as a later version may add fields. A reader of the say messages alone skips every `unknown` frame, the other link messages, the room's and the reach messages among them; every `malformed` frame is refused. Each of `names` is a name as a player gives it (typed, or sent by the client when a marked speaker's name is clicked), and `names` the name it gives once the mark a line said from Discord shows beside its speaker is taken off. In a frame, `${c*N}` stands for the character c written N times.",
